Let \(p(z)\) be given by the rule
\begin{equation*}
p(z) = \frac{z\tan(z)}{z^2\sec(z) + 1} + 3 e^z + 1\text{.}
\end{equation*}
Determine \(p'(z)\text{.}\)
Find an equation for the tangent line to \(p\) at the point where \(z = 0\text{.}\)
At \(z = 0\text{,}\) is \(p\) increasing, decreasing, or neither? Why?
